/-!
# KFW: the exponent expressions of the uniform phase passes

The uniform phase pass `phLU … εE` reads, in iteration `k` (index on `kS`), the exponent
`εE = aE k mod 4`.  For the stride-`K` layouts of the level procedure,
`pos i = e - K φ(i)` with `φ : ι ≃ Fin N`, so

  `aEof pos a' p = if p ≤ e ∧ K ∣ e - p ∧ (e - p)/K < N then a' (φ⁻¹ ((e-p)/K)) else 0`

